      "text": "An empty tree usually means pegging relations were never generated. The vendor treats generation as a precondition: relations come from Update Pegging Relations during the planning run (step 3 of Run MRP) or from Generate Pegging Relations (cprrp0240m000), and LN only generates them out to the Pegging Horizon in Planning Parameters (cprpd0100m000) — cpordplanug, \"Pegging for planned orders\" (p. 113–114). In the observed environment this is not a risk: Update Pegging Relations is locked on, evidenced 2026-08-25 — see Run MRP's notes. Yours may differ, and the check is the greyed-or-not state of that box, not its tick."
    }
  ],
  "why": {
    "tokens": [
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "The pegging tree walks the relations the run recorded: upstream, what will supply this demand; downstream, what demand caused this order. The tree exists only if pegging relations were generated, which in this environment happens on every run because the option is locked on."
      }
    ],
